# A builtin called with the wrong number of arguments.
#
# `print` takes any number, but the other three do not: `string` turns one
# value into a String. Their arities are checked at the call, which is
# the only place a builtin may appear.
#
# This program is expected to FAIL type checking. Its `.out` holds the
# error message, not a program's output.

text = string(1, 2)
